translated_text:
Part Two

Prevention of Acts of Violence

Article 6

(1) The Regional Government shall prevent acts of violence against women by means of:

a. socializing laws and regulations;
b. conducting empowerment and awareness raising to families, parents and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling; c. undertaking efforts to increase the quantity and quality of formal, non-formal and informal education;
d. undertaking efforts to build community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection of women and children from violence in an integrated community-based manner;
e. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement officials, government officials, universities, religious institutions/organizations and various civil society organizations in efforts to prevent violence against women and children;
f. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to violence;
g. raising community awareness that respects women and protects children;
h. establishing UPTD PPA in every Sub-district, and Protection Service Posts for Women and Children at the Village and Sub-district levels; and
i. establishing a task force for the protection of women and children.
(2) In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community;
c. vertical agencies;
d. law enforcement officials;
e. educational institutions;
f. health institutions;
g. religious institutions/organizations;
h. community social institutions;
1. business sector; and
j. other institutions.
(3) Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in an integrated manner and coordinated by the Regional Apparatus having the principal tasks and functions in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

