translated_text:
Part Three

Integrated Services for Victims of Acts of Violence

Article 8

(1) The Regional Government shall implement integrated services for victims of acts of violence, through activities:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. counseling;
d. psychological services;
e. spiritual guidance;
f. social rehabilitation services;
g. legal aid and assistance services;
h. safe house services; and/or
i. repatriation and social reintegration.
(2) In the event that the Regional Government does not yet have counseling personnel as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c, it may request assistance from social workers, volunteer assistants, and/or spiritual advisors.
(3) The services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:
a. special service rooms in police ranks;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses; and/or
d. other facilities and infrastructure needed for the recovery of victims including perpetrators.
(4) The provision of services to victims of acts of violence shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with other social institutions. (5) Other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (4) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner. (6) Integrated services for victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (5) shall be implemented in accordance with standard operating procedures.
(7) Provisions regarding standard operating procedures as referred to in paragraph (6) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

Article 9

(1) Complaint services as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (1) letter a shall be implemented to receive reports of acts of violence.

(2) Reports as referred to in paragraph (1) may originate from: a. victims;

b. referrals; or

c. outreach.

