(6) Untuk setiap tindakan medis yang akan dilakukan oleh tenaga kesehatan harus ada persetujuan tindakan medis dari korban atau keluarganya sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang-undangan.

(7) Untuk keperluan penyidikan, tenaga kesehatan yang berwenang harus membuat visum et repertum dan / atau visum et repertum psichiatricum. atau membuat surat keterangan medis.

(8) Tenaga kesehatan berhak mendapatkan perlindungan hukum.

translated_text:
Article 10

(1) Health services as referred to in Article 8 paragraph - (1) letter b, shall be implemented using health facilities owned by the Regional Government or other referral hospitals by providing medical treatment and health recovery services for victims.

(2) Health services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be performed by health personnel to victims in accordance with professional standards, operational procedure standards and the medical needs of victims.

(3) Health services as referred to in paragraph (1), through efforts: a. anamnesis of victims;

b. examination of victims;

c. providing first aid;

d. recovery of physical and psychological health, undertaking efforts to prevent disease and other health disorders;

e. counseling;

f. referring to more adequate health service facilities if necessary, may refer to other parties with a multidisciplinary approach, including health services, medicolegal, psychosocial assistance and legal aid; and/or

g. providing information to the police.

(4) In addition to the efforts as referred to in paragraph (3) for certain cases, health personnel may provide reproductive health services in accordance with medical needs.

(5) In providing services as referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4), health personnel must maintain medical records in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(6) For every medical action to be performed by health personnel, there must be informed consent for medical action from the victim or their family in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

(7) For the purposes of investigation, authorized health personnel must prepare a visum et repertum and/or visum et repertum psichiatricum or prepare a medical certificate.

(8) Health personnel are entitled to legal protection.

